{
  "borough": "Harrow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;The proposal would fail to retain the\r\ncharacter and appearance of the existing dwelling and the street scene and would\r\ntherefore fail to accord with&amp;nbsp; National\r\nPlanning Policy Framework (2023), Policy D3 of the London Plan (2021), Core\r\nPolicy CS1 (B) of the Harrow Core Strategy (2012), policy DM 1 of the Harrow\r\nDevelopment Management Policies Local Plan (2013) and the adopted Supplementary\r\nPlanning Document: Residential Design Guide (2010).&lt;font face=&quot;Arial, sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "The proposal fails to make any provision for external amenity space from the upper floor flat and thus provides an inadequate standard of amenity for the future occupiers. As such, the proposal is contrary to Policies D3 and D6 of The London Plan and&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%;&quot;&gt;Paragraph 5.16 of the Harrow Residential Design Guide SPD 2010.&lt;/span&gt;",
    "The proposal fails to provide adequate provision for parking within the curtilage of the property. Given the high demand for on-street parking and the increased demand for such parking as a result of the intensified use, the use is likely to have an adverse effect on highway safety and movement, contrary to&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%;&quot;&gt;policies T5, T6, T6.1 of The London Plan (2021)\r\nand policy DM42 of the Harrow Development Management Policies Local Plan\r\n(2013).&lt;/span&gt;"
  ],
